>YER069W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:V:295410:298001:1 gene:YER069W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:ARG5,6 description:Acetylglutamate kinase and N-acetyl-gamma-glutamyl-phosphate reductase; N-acetyl-L-glutamate kinase (NAGK) catalyzes the 2nd and N-acetyl-gamma-glutamyl-phosphate reductase (NAGSA), the 3rd step in arginine biosynthesis; synthesized as a precursor which is processed in the mitochondrion to yield mature NAGK and NAGSA; enzymes form a metabolon complex with Arg2p; NAGK C-terminal domain stabilizes the enzymes, slows catalysis and is involved in feed-back inhibition by arginine [Source:SGD;Acc:S000000871]
