>YEL062W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:V:34407:36254:1 gene:YEL062W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:NPR2 description:Subunit of the Iml1p/SEACIT complex; SEACIT (Iml1p-Npr2p-Npr3p) is a subcomplex of the SEA complex, a coatomer-related complex that associates dynamically with the vacuole; Npr2p may have a structural or regulatory role, supporting Iml1p function as a GAP for the Rag family GTPase Gtr1p, and resulting in inhibition of TORC1 signaling in response to amino acid deprivation; SEACIT is required for non-nitrogen-starvation-induced autophagy; homolog of human tumor suppressor NPRL2 [Source:SGD;Acc:S000000788]
