>YOL138C_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:XV:61325:65350:-1 gene:YOL138C gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:RTC1 description:Subunit of SEACAT, a subcomplex of the SEA complex; Rtc1p, along with Mtc5p and Sea4p, redundantly inhibit the TORC1 inhibitory role of the Iml1p/SEACIT (Iml1p-Npr2p-Npr3p) subcomplex, a GAP for GTPase Gtr1p (EGOC subunit) in response to amino acid limitation, thereby resulting in activation of TORC1 signaling; SEA is a coatomer-related complex that associates dynamically with the vacuole; has N-terminal WD-40 repeats and a C-terminal RING motif; null suppresses cdc13-1 [Source:SGD;Acc:S000005498]
