>YDR128W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:IV:709549:712995:1 gene:YDR128W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:MTC5 description:Subunit of SEACAT, a subcomplex of the SEA complex; Mtc1p, along with Rtc1p and Sea4p, redundantly inhibit the TORC1 inhibitory role of the Iml1p/SEACIT (Iml1p-Npr2p-Npr3p) subcomplex, a GAP for GTPase Gtr1p (EGOC subunit) in response to amino acid limitation, thereby resulting in activation of TORC1 signaling; SEA is a coatomer-related complex that associates dynamically with the vacuole; relative distribution to the vacuolar membrane decreases upon DNA replication stress [Source:SGD;Acc:S000002535]
