>YDR477W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:IV:1412373:1414274:1 gene:YDR477W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:SNF1 description:AMP-activated S/T protein kinase; forms a complex with Snf4p and members of the Sip1p/Sip2p/Gal83p family; required for transcription of glucose-repressed genes, thermotolerance, sporulation, and peroxisome biogenesis; regulates nucleocytoplasmic shuttling of Hxk2p; regulates filamentous growth and acts as a non-canonical GEF, activating Arf3p during invasive growth; SUMOylation by Mms21p inhibits its function and targets Snf1p for destruction via the Slx5-Slx8 Ub ligase [Source:SGD;Acc:S000002885]
