>YER120W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:V:401135:401869:1 gene:YER120W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:SCS2 description:Integral ER membrane protein, regulates phospholipid metabolism; one of 6 proteins (Ist2p, Scs2p, Scs22p, Tcb1p, Tcb2p, Tcb3p) that connect ER to plasma membrane (PM) and regulate PI4P levels by controlling access of Sac1p phosphatase to substrate PI4P in the PM; interacts with FFAT motifs in Opi1p, Swh1p, Osh2p, and Osh3p; involved in telomeric silencing; VAP homolog; SCS2 has a paralog, SCS22, that arose from the whole genome duplication [Source:SGD;Acc:S000000922]
