>YER008C_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:V:167808:171818:-1 gene:YER008C gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:SEC3 description:Subunit of the exocyst complex; the exocyst mediates polarized targeting and tethering of post-Golgi secretory vesicles to sites of exocytosis prior to SNARE-mediated fusion; PtdIns[4,5]P2-binding protein that localizes to exocytic sites in a Rho1p-dependent, actin-independent manner, targeting and anchoring the exocyst to the plasma membrane with Exo70p; direct GTP Rho1p effector; required for ER inheritance; relocalizes away from bud neck upon DNA replication stress [Source:SGD;Acc:S000000810]
