>YEL071W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:V:16355:17845:1 gene:YEL071W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:DLD3 description:2-hydroxyglutarate transhydrogenase, and minor D-lactate dehydrogenase; converts D-2-hydroxyglutarate (D-2HG), an oncometabolite, to alpha-ketoglutarate in the presence of FAD, with concomitant reduction of pyruvate to D-lactate; minor lactate dehydrogenase activity; component of the retrograde regulon that consists of genes whose expression are stimulated by damage to mitochondria and reduced in cells grown with glutamate as the sole nitrogen source; located in the cytoplasm [Source:SGD;Acc:S000000797]
