>YBL104C_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:II:18177:21293:-1 gene:YBL104C gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:SEA4 description:Subunit of SEACAT, a subcomplex of the SEA complex; Sea4p, along with Rtc1p and Mtc5p, redundantly inhibit the TORC1 inhibitory role of the Iml1p/SEACIT (Iml1p-Npr2p-Npr3p) subcomplex, a GAP for GTPase Gtr1p (EGOC subunit) in response to amino acid limitation, thereby resulting in activation of TORC1 signaling; SEA is a coatomer-related complex that associates dynamically with the vacuole; contains an N-terminal beta-propeller fold and a C-terminal RING motif [Source:SGD;Acc:S000000200]
