>YGL071W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:VII:372012:374084:1 gene:YGL071W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:AFT1 description:Transcription factor involved in iron utilization and homeostasis; binds consensus site PyPuCACCCPu and activates transcription in response to changes in iron availability; in iron-replete conditions localization is regulated by Grx3p, Grx4p, and Fra2p, and promoter binding is negatively regulated via Grx3p-Grx4p binding; AFT1 has a paralog, AFT2, that arose from the whole genome duplication; relative distribution to the nucleus increases upon DNA replication stress [Source:SGD;Acc:S000003039]
