>YDR121W_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:IV:693585:694175:1 gene:YDR121W gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:DPB4 description:Subunit of DNA pol epsilon and of ISW2 chromatin accessibility complex; involved in both chromosomal DNA replication and inheritance of telomeric silencing; stabilizes the interaction of Pol epsilon with primer-template DNA, positively affecting the processivity of the polymerase and exonuclease activities of Pol epsilon; interacts with extranucleosomal DNA and acts as anchor point for ISW2 complex that retains its position on DNA during nucleosome mobilization [Source:SGD;Acc:S000002528]
