>YJL141C_mRNA cds chromosome:R64-1-1:X:147967:150390:-1 gene:YJL141C gene_biotype:protein_coding transcript_biotype:protein_coding gene_symbol:YAK1 description:Serine-threonine protein kinase; component of a glucose-sensing system that inhibits growth in response to glucose availability; upon nutrient deprivation Yak1p phosphorylates Pop2p to regulate mRNA deadenylation, the co-repressor Crf1p to inhibit transcription of ribosomal genes, and the stress-responsive transcription factors Hsf1p and Msn2p; nuclear localization negatively regulated by the Ras/PKA signaling pathway in the presence of glucose [Source:SGD;Acc:S000003677]
